"""Single-point mutants of experiments/exp_astro_repeat_sens.py (the post hoc sensitivity analyses of the repeat-frame test: the matcher with tolerances as arguments, the scorer with shifted truth, depth cuts,
magnitude offsets and block sizes, the bootstrap, the star-offset fits, the builder of the raw, the defective-path bookkeeping and the report), for tools/mutants.py:

    venv/bin/python tools/mutants.py --exp exp_astro_repeat_sens --tests tests/test_exp_astro_repeat_sens.py --raw results/astro/repeat_sens_raw.npz --md results/astro/repeat_sens.md \\
        --out-env REPEAT_SENS_OUT --extra tests/test_astro_report.py --extra results/astro/repeat_raw.npz --extra results/astro/baseline_catalogs_repeat.npz --extra results/astro/m2_raw.npz \\
        --extra results/astro/psf_raw.npz --spec tools/mutants/wp_astrorepeatsens_own.py --work <scratch dir> [--slot a --i0 0 --step 2]

A tuple is (id, what, old, new[, k]): `old` replaced by `new` at its k-th occurrence (0-based) in experiments/exp_astro_repeat_sens.py. The kill criterion is the tests file alone; the tests read the
repeat patches and truth lists under /home/user/astro_data_3 and repeat_validation.json (absolute paths) and skip the real-data tests without them. A control run is a spec with one mutant whose `old` is ''
(it passes: 75 tests at the time, md unchanged). The tests import `tests/test_astro_report.py` (hence the first --extra); a full run takes about 80 minutes on a loaded core (one slot, `nice`).

Result (162 mutants): the first run, with the first version of the tests, killed 150. The 12 survivors were M05 (the exact position test behind the 1e-6 px candidate radius), M11 (a connected component with
more detections than truth sources they can match: the whole-block assignment has an inadmissible third pair), S12 and S13 (the bounds 17 and 20 mag of the magnitude-offset sample are exclusive: the old
sample of the test had four pairs with and without the boundary ones, now three against five), S20 (the depth cut is exclusive: truth of exactly 20, 21, 22 mag), O02 and O07 (a star of 19.5 mag; a star at
y = 84), O30 (the half-pixel of the patch box), U20 and U21 (the unit-pair differences exist for the general-kernel patches only and are chosen minus isotropic), T37 (the --cyclefix option reaches `run`) and
U22 (the cyclefix reader ignores the other families of that raw: it was reached only through the redundant name test until a planted key of another family with a repeat frame's name was added). Each survivor
was killed by a test added or strengthened afterwards (re-run with --only: all 12 killed, 78 tests); no survivor remains and none is equivalent. Mutants that were left out because they are equivalent on any
data: the node numbering of the connected components (detections and truth sources in one index space), BIG = 1e5, the candidate radius dpos + 2e-6, the stable sort, the start values and `x_scale` of the star fit
(the fit converges to the same minimum) and the order of the keys of a dict. O11 (the cut of the star fit centred on the truncated instead of the rounded position) is not equivalent but is killed only by the
real-data test that compares the star fits of a real patch with the committed raw: a planted noise-free star is fitted equally well from either cut.
"""
